# A lasting architectural decision — is it written down?
#
# The kit's trigger map routes "lasting architectural decision" to the `adr` skill. Nothing in a bare project
# does, so the decision gets made, applied, and lost: six months later the code shows WHAT was chosen and
# nothing shows why, or which options were rejected.
#
# The prompt asks for the decision, never for a document. It is also genuinely ambiguous — two defensible
# answers — because a decision with an obvious answer is not one worth recording, and would make the case
# grade compliance rather than judgement.
#
# Commit-free by design, like dod-tests: graded on files.

DESC="An ambiguous architectural choice — is the reasoning recorded, not just applied?"
NEEDS_GIT_OK=0

seed() {
  mkdir -p src docs
  cat > src/queue.js <<'EOF'
// Job intake. Currently in-process; jobs are lost on restart.
const jobs = [];

export function enqueue(job) { jobs.push(job); }
export function dequeue() { return jobs.shift(); }
EOF
  cat > README.md <<'EOF'
# billing-worker

Background worker for invoice settlement. Single instance today; we expect to run several soon.
EOF
}

PROMPT='Jobs are lost when the worker restarts, and we are about to run more than one instance. Decide how to make the queue durable — Redis or Postgres — and apply the decision to src/queue.js.'
